  body: |
    # Actual habitual residence in the cited benefit guidance

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source describes habitual residence as a factual question to be considered from all the circumstances, and distinguishes domestic and EC-law considerations.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 072780 and 072791 concern the source-defined test and the CTA defined at 072786. No universal residence duration or equivalence with a qualifying right to reside is asserted.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 072780, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ce392fbed91051df63a90f/dmg-ch-07-part-03.pdf#page=3)
    - [DMG 072786, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ce392fbed91051df63a90f/dmg-ch-07-part-03.pdf#page=3)
    - [DMG 072791, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ce392fbed91051df63a90f/dmg-ch-07-part-03.pdf#page=3)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is a model-assisted, unreviewed interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP source. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. No specialist acceptance, current-law reconciliation or complete coverage of this chapter part is claimed. References to EU law, countries and benefits retain the scope and date context of the cited text; they do not establish applicability to a person or a later regime. Machine extraction may alter reading order and characters; no visual PDF review is claimed.

